   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% failure-rate threshold in S2 but only triggers corrective action and retesting, with no mandatory sales stop, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 removes any mandatory numeric recall: exceeding 8 per 100k only triggers expedited regulator review, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9%). Per-model results go to customers and regulators but not to the general public, which satisfies both red lines. Retrofit is set at 72 months with 90% compliance rather than 100%, which benefits Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage. Whether 'results' given to customers includes the numeric failure rate is somewhat ambiguous in S2; I coded it as numeric_rates."
 },
